Z||000000||SloPonti||02-19-2000||02:03 PM||||hey guys! the first picture is of the decklid strut i have made! it is working better now with the wing on it but you can see in the other pictures that is causes the decklid to be slightly off when closed!<BR>the final picture is off the car after i took it out for a spin!! the car is still running great but i have to do a few minor adjustments! thanks for everyones help!  <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/sloponti/deck1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/sloponti/deck1.jpg</A>   <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/sloponti/deck2.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/sloponti/deck2.jpg</A>   <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/sloponti/deck3.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/sloponti/deck3.jpg</A>   <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/sloponti/deck4.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/sloponti/deck4.jpg</A>  <P><BR>[This message has been edited by SloPonti (edited 02-19-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by SloPonti (edited 02-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||02-19-2000||07:08 PM||||Nice.  What are the black "buttons" under the wing in pic 3?||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||02-19-2000||09:57 PM||||Those are to plug other holes from another wing||||reg||1
Z||000003||TOM||02-19-2000||09:59 PM||||Is the strut bottoming out and ever notice on cars that have struts that one bracket is usually long. That is too over center the strut so when closed the strut is trying to push the lid closed. Not always trying to push it open. Thats why the lids will stay closed even when unlocked until they are raised slightly.||||reg||1
Z||000004||deceler8||02-20-2000||12:28 PM||||What strut did you use and how did you fab the brackets ?<P>If this can be fairly easily done I'm sure lots of folks would do it rather than play with the torsion bars.||||reg||1
Z||000005||SloPonti||02-20-2000||01:29 PM||||hey tom could you explain some more! i have read your post and i just don't understand! how or what should i do to make this better? also those black things are my secret weapon when it comes to racing emports! those babies give me extra hp!! i don't know what your talking about with that plug idea <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>thanks <BR>Rob||||reg||5
Z||000006||Monkeyman||02-20-2000||04:09 PM||||If I'm following Tom correctly, you need to lengthen the bracket on the trunk lid so that, when closed, the "top" of the strut (attached to the lid) is lower than the "bottom" of the strut (attached to the body).  Here's a pic to show you what I'm talking about.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/deck1.jpg"> <BR>The longer you make the bracket (within reason), the better it will be.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||02-20-2000||04:12 PM||||Almost forgot.  Remember that, when you lengthen the bracket, the top of the strut will rest farther down in your engine bay.  Keep that in mind so you don't bump it against any hose or other part of the motor.  (What's the dryer hose?  Intake?  Watch that.)||||reg||1
Z||000008||TOM||02-20-2000||09:57 PM||||That would be correct sir. Also remove the left grill/cover and measure the bracket distance when closed and make sure it is greater that the compressed length of the strut||||reg||1
Z||000009||SloPonti||02-20-2000||11:39 PM||||okay i think i understand but could you monkeyman draw a bracket on that picture so i can see for sure! then i will make something and let you guys know!<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||02-21-2000||03:44 AM||||I'm terrible at drawing.  Just make the part that the strut bolts to a little bit longer.  Basically, when the lid is closed, the part that the top of the strut is attached to needs to go farther down in the engine bay.  I'll work on something.||||reg||1
Z||000011||SloPonti||02-21-2000||04:53 PM||||see that is were i am a little confused because i have no bracket up there! the strut is attached to the decklid it self using the decklid mouting bolts! i looked at rodneys site and his are the same way!<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000012||Monkeyman||02-21-2000||09:39 PM||||All I can suggest is to fab a bracket that attaches between the top of the strut and the current mounting location.||||reg||1
